    "contract": "assurance_kernel/task_intent/v1",
    "task_id": "wcr-terminal-tracker-mutation-safety",
    "goal": "Stop kernel_ports.ts's terminal-tracker projection from running inside the authorize try/catch that owns Kernel-mutation rollback: a projection failure after the underlying Kernel mutation has already committed must never trigger restoreStagedIntent() or rethrow in a way a caller could read as 'the mutation did not happen' and retry.",
    "acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "RB3-1",
        "assertion": "In runtime/claude/kernel_ports.ts's authorize path, a forced failure inside the terminal-tracker projection (withTerminalTracker) that runs after app.execute has already committed the operation (op: 'stop', 'authorize_rework', or 'approve_breaking_intent_revision') does not call restoreStagedIntent() and does not cause the caller to receive an exception implying the underlying mutation did not apply; the mutation's committed result is still returned, with the tracker failure reported alongside it (not as an authority-level error).",
        "verification": "{\n  \"contract\": \"assurance_kernel/verification_descriptor/v1\",\n  \"runner_id\": \"bun\",\n  \"runner_version\": \"1.4.2\",\n  \"argv\": [\n    \"test\",\n    \"tests/claude-batch-authority.test.ts\",\n    \"tests/kernel-batch-authority.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"cwd\": \".\",\n  \"timeout_ms\": 120000,\n  \"max_output_bytes\": 131072\n}\n"
      }
